(5978527, 871605, 50695, '<td valign="top">Lovely. This got a 5 from me, which is equal to my combined score for the other two ribbon-winners.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-04-28 23:59:30.</i></td>', 'Lovely. This got a 5 from me, which is equal to my combined score for the other two ribbon-winners.', '2010-04-29 00:58:19.000000', '2010-04-29 00:59:30.000000', 0),
(5978713, 869888, 91360, '<td valign="top">Hi Mark,<br/>I really like the concept.<br/>I think that in order to get more sharpness in the front and details in the circle waves, you should have use a MACRO 60MM lense, in addition, the position and the angel of the feather in the frame is a little bit far for me.<br/></td>', 'Hi Mark,I really like the concept.I think that in order to get more sharpness in the front and details in the circle waves, you should have use a MACRO 60MM lense, in addition, the position and the angel of the feather in the frame is a little bit far for me.', '2010-04-29 05:44:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5978732, 869127, 115345, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Sevlow:</b></div><hr/><i> Interesting, and I do like it but what does ACW mean? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>ACW = All Comments Welcome... have tried it a few times recently to see if it will up my comment quota but don''t think it works except to generate comments like ''what does ACW stand for''!... :)<br/> <br/>cheers<br/> <br/>Jon</td>', 'Originally posted by Sevlow: Interesting, and I do like it but what does ACW mean?   ACW = All Comments Welcome... have tried it a few times recently to see if it will up my comment quota but don''t think it works except to generate comments like ''what does ACW stand for''!... :) cheers Jon', '2010-04-29 05:55:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5978734, 870846, 116375, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by scooter97:</b></div><hr/><i> I own that book. Should have been a motorcycle, not a bicycle. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>There''s absolutely no reason why it couldn''t be a bicycle instead -the idea wasn''t to stick religiously to the title of the book, just to show where the inspiration came from.</td>', 'Originally posted by scooter97: I own that book. Should have been a motorcycle, not a bicycle.   There''s absolutely no reason why it couldn''t be a bicycle instead -the idea wasn''t to stick religiously to the title of the book, just to show where the inspiration came from.', '2010-04-29 05:56:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5978735, 871360, 91360, '<td valign="top">:)</td>', ':)', '2010-04-29 05:59:11.000000', NULL, 0);
